  "notes": "The UK crossover record: an afrobeats pocket played on trap production. The kick keeps the bounce the compendium writes as 1 and 2.75 — beat 1 always, then the 'a' of 2 — with a light 2-and-4 snare and a rim answering it, so it never one-drops the way dancehall does. What separates it from both parents is on top and underneath: a continuous 16th hat carpet with rolls, and a warm 808 sliding at phrase ends, neither of which afrobeats or dancehall has. Swing sits at 0.57, between the straight grid trap works on and the heavy shuffle of garage. Harmony is minor with the light on — Dorian as often as natural minor, sevenths on nearly everything, four-chord loops that turn over rather than resolve — and the topline is sung, mid-high, two-bar question answered by a two-bar answer, with shakers and congas thinner than an afrobeats mix would carry them.",
